id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, EngineError> with TS's message; panic only on invariants (ReduceResult.error is Option<String>)
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn(&mut EffectContext) -> Vec<Effect> + Send + Sync> via hook(); triggers via TriggerDef::new(..).with_when(..); no fn pointers, no Box
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state; tests use the testkit's thread-local register_scripts over a clone of registered_scripts()
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
test.live_objects: owned CardInstance copies; writes through find_instance_mut(s.state_mut(), id)
test.card_refs: &str (catalog id, index, name, or an instance's id)
test.scenario_state_mut: Scenario::state_mut() -> &mut GameState (not in SURFACE §8's table)
test.default_params: scalar default -> trailing Option<T>; anonymous options object -> local struct with Default
test.fixture_defs: CardDef built with json_as(json!(TS literal)) and inserted into state.transient_defs
test.literals: actions json_as::<ActionInput>/json_as::<Action>(json!), effect args json_as(json!)
